  "panel_reasoning_excerpt": "## TEMPLATE 16: DT_RESTORATION_TIMECOURSE_001\n**\"Transition to restorative environment \u2192 DMN re-engagement timecourse\"**\n\n**Structural pattern**: state_transition \u2192 recovery_dynamics \u2192 temporal_profile\n**Transferable to**: Any transition from high-demand to low-demand context\n\n**Causal chain**:\n1. Exit from high-demand environment \u2192 removal of sustained attentional demands\n   - Level: ecological \u2192 computational\n   - Maturity: **how-actually**\n2. TPN deactivation \u2192 DMN re-engagement (not instantaneous \u2014 requires ~5-15 min)\n   - Level: circuit\n   - Maturity: **how-plausibly**\n   - Parameter range: Initial DMN re-engagement detectable within ~3-5 min (fMRI); full restoration of baseline DMN-TPN balance ~20-40 min; individual variation substantial (correlated with mindfulness trait scores)\n3. DMN re-engagement \u2192 parasympathetic shift \u2192 cortisol recovery \u2192 subjective restoration experience\n   - Level: circuit \u2192 systems \u2192 psychological\n   - Maturity: **how-plausibly**\n   - Parameter range: Cortisol recovery half-life ~60 min; subjective restoration reported at ~20-30 min\n\n**Predictions**:\n- Brief nature exposure (<5 min) should produce measurable perceptual benefits (PP_SPECTRAL_MATCH_001 operates fast) but NOT full restoration benefits (which require DMN re-engagement)\n- Full restoration requires ~20-40 min in a low-demand environment\n- Individual differences in restoration speed should correlate with DMN-TPN switching efficiency (measurable via fMRI)\n\n**Overall maturity**: **how-plausibly**\n\n---",
